# LIFE-LINK Development Rules

## General
- Use TypeScript. Strict mode.
- Reuse existing components. Do not duplicate.
- Keep functions small. Single responsibility.
- Do not modify unrelated files. Focused changes.
- Follow DESIGN.md exactly.

## Before Coding
- Read relevant docs
- Inspect existing code
- Reuse functionality where possible
- Make a plan for large changes

## UI
- Follow DESIGN.md
- Mobile responsive (375px, 768px, 1440px)
- Include loading states
- Include error states
- Include empty states
- Accessible: ARIA labels, semantic HTML

## Security
- Never expose API keys
- Validate user input server-side
- Verify authorization
- Check roles before operations

## Testing
- Add tests for important features
- Run tests after implementation
- Fix failing tests before merging

## Git
- Small commits
- Descriptive messages: 'feat: add emergency matching'
- Branch per feature

